  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Electronic configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ce</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><munder><munder><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&#9183;</mo></munder><mrow></mrow></munder><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo></msup></mrow></mover><munder><munder><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><mo>&#9183;</mo></munder><mrow></mrow></munder></math></p><p>Cerium in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> oxidation state due to stable xenon configuration.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>La</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Lu</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Gd</mi></math>&nbsp;are stable in +3 oxidation state.</p>"
